-- title:
--   Hecke eigencharacter lifting a maximal ideal of T^S
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$, let $S$ be a set of natural numbers, and let $\mathbb{T}^S =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\,S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. Let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathbb{T}^S$. The assertion is that there exist a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ and an ideal $\mathfrak{M}$ of `integralClosure ℤ ℂ`, the ring of algebraic integers in $\mathbb{C}$, such that: $g$ satisfies `IsNormalizedEigenform`, i.e. its $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff g n` satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\,a_{p^r}$ for primes $p \nmid N$ and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for primes $p \mid N$; $\mathfrak{M}$ is maximal; and for every $t \in \mathbb{T}^S$ there is an algebraic integer $a$ with $t\,g = a \cdot g$ as elements of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, such that $t \in \mathfrak{m}$ implies $a \in \mathfrak{M}$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma in Hecke-ring form: a maximal ideal of the weight-$2$ Hecke ring of level $N$ is cut out by reducing, modulo a maximal ideal of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$, the eigencharacter of a characteristic-zero normalised eigenform. It is used to produce the residual Galois representation attached to a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra, and thence the residual modularity of a Frey curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_of_isMaximal_heckeAlgebra.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_of_isMaximal_heckeAlgebra (N : ℕ) [NeZero N]
    (S : Set ℕ) (𝔪 : Ideal (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S)) (h𝔪 : 𝔪.IsMaximal) :
    ∃ (g : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2) (𝔐 : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ ℂ)),
      g.IsNormalizedEigenform ∧ 𝔐.IsMaximal ∧
      ∀ t : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S, ∃ a : integralClosure ℤ ℂ,
        (t : Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2)) g = (a : ℂ) • g ∧
        (t ∈ 𝔪 → a ∈ 𝔐) := by sorry
